.TH KEEP-RAM-CLEAN 1 "November 2026" "keep-ram-clean 2.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keep-ram-clean \- configurable Linux RAM, tmpfs, swap, and memory-pressure management daemon and CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keep-ram-clean
[\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keep-ram-clean
monitors Linux memory telemetry from \fI/proc/meminfo\fR, Pressure Stall Information
(\fI/proc/pressure/memory\fR), \fI/proc/swaps\fR, and \fI/proc/mounts\fR, and executes
safe, modular memory reclamation actions only when user-configured thresholds,
intervals, or cron schedules are triggered.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-watch\fR [\fB\-\-view config\fR]] [\fB\-\-interval\fR \fISECS\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Display a dashboard of RAM, swap, tmpfs mounts, PSI contention, top memory
consumers, auto-clean triggers, and recent cleanup activity. In \fB\-\-watch\fR mode,
interactive hotkeys allow triggering cleanups (\fBc\fR), adjusting RAM trigger
thresholds (\fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR), toggling desktop notifications (\fBn\fR), reloading
config (\fBr\fR), and quitting (\fBq\fR).
Press \fBs\fR to open Settings, or start there with \fB\-\-view config\fR.
Settings reports the current file or built-in values and previews a physical-RAM
preset for the available-RAM floor. In an editable file, \fBe\fR opens the
editor, \fBj\fR/\fBk\fR select a field, and Enter stages a manually entered
value. On Available floor, \fBp\fR stages the preset. Use \fBw\fR to review
every change, then Enter to save. Saving does not signal or reload the daemon.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fISTEPS\fR] [\fB\-\-critical\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
Execute a one-shot cleanup immediately. Valid steps: \fBtmpfs\fR, \fBwatchdog\fR,
\fBuser_caches\fR, \fBkernel\fR, \fBswap\fR.
.TP
.B daemon \fR[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Start the background monitoring and cleanup daemon. Supports \fBSIGHUP\fR for live
config reload and \fBSIGUSR1\fR for immediate on-demand cleanup.
.TP
.B config show \fR| \fBconfig set \fIKEY VALUE\fR
Inspect or update auto-clean trigger and notification settings in \fIconfig.toml\fR
and automatically hot-reload the running daemon.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Audit Linux kernel VM configuration including PSI, cgroup v2 \fImemory.reclaim\fR,
MGLRU, zram/zswap, \fIvm.swappiness\fR, and \fIvm.vfs_cache_pressure\fR.
.TP
.B init-config \fR[\fB\-o\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-f\fR]
Generate a documented starter \fIconfig.toml\fR.
.TP
.B trigger \fR| \fBreload\fR
Send \fBSIGUSR1\fR (immediate cleanup) or \fBSIGHUP\fR (reload config) to the running
daemon using Linux \fIpidfd\fR verification.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/keep-ram-clean/config.toml
System-wide configuration file (used exclusively in root/system mode).
.TP
.I ~/.config/keep-ram-clean/config.toml
Per-user configuration file (used in non-root user mode).
